      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Long-distance quantum communication made entanglement distribution and quantum links experimentally credible, creating a major quantum-optics capability.",
        "attribution": "Gisin's group established essential long-distance fiber demonstrations, while Pan drove landmark free-space and satellite-scale entanglement distribution.",
        "maturity": "The underlying experiments have been repeatedly verified and have developed into an active international technology field.",
        "uncertainties": [
