        "Antoine Browaeys",
        "Mark Saffman",
        "Mikhail D. Lukin"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Programmable Rydberg arrays offer direct control of interacting many-body systems and a powerful route to quantum simulation and processing.",
        "attribution": "Saffman established important Rydberg-gate concepts, while Browaeys and Lukin led decisive programmable-array experiments.",
        "maturity": "Experimental control and system sizes have advanced rapidly, with reproducible demonstrations across several laboratories.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "Its full long-term scientific and technological impact remains less settled than that of older quantum platforms."
        ]
